      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0191",
      "sequence": 203,
      "meaning": "On the sacred ninth lunar day of the spring month, in the bright fortnight under the auspicious Abhijit, at midday when it is neither cold nor hot, the holy hour brings repose to the world. A cool, gentle, fragrant wind blows; gods and saints rejoice; forests bloom, mountains gleam with jewels, and every river pours nectar-like water. Knowing the moment, Brahmā and all the gods mount their aerial cars. The pure sky fills with celestial hosts: Gandharvas sing, flowers rain from lovely handfuls, and heavenly drums resound. Nāgas, sages and gods offer praise and many forms of service, then return home after their petition. The Lord who houses the universe manifests as the repose of every world.",
