    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0193",
      "sequence": 205,
      "meaning": "Hearing the infant’s supremely sweet cry, all the queens rush in agitation; maids hurry from every side and all Ayodhyā is submerged in joy. When Daśaratha hears of his son’s birth, he experiences Brahman-bliss: his body thrills with deepest love, and he tries to rise while steadying his mind. The Lord whose name itself makes auspiciousness has entered his home. Filled with supreme joy, the king orders music to sound and summons Guru Vasiṣṭha, who arrives at the palace gate with Brahmins. They behold the incomparable child, whose store of beauty and virtues cannot be exhausted in speech, then perform the Nāndīmukha ancestral rite and every birth ceremony. The king gives Brahmins gold, cows, garments and jewels.",
