      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0194",
      "sequence": 206,
      "meaning": "Flags, banners and festal arches cover the exquisitely decorated city as flowers rain from the sky and everyone is absorbed in divine joy. Groups of women, naturally adorned, rise and hurry together carrying golden pitchers and auspicious trays while singing into the palace. They wave lamps, offer gifts against the evil eye, and repeatedly fall at the infant’s feet. Bards, genealogists, panegyrists and singers celebrate Raghunātha’s purifying virtues. The king gives away all his wealth; recipients keep none of what they receive. Musk, sandalwood and vermilion form festive mud throughout the streets. Auspicious music sounds in every home, for the root of beauty has appeared, and all groups of women and men rejoice throughout the city.",
